evidence_at_head:
frontend/src/app.css:156-161 at HEAD is verbatim `#app {
 max-width: 1280px;
 margin: 0 auto;
 padding: 2rem;
 text-align: center;
}` — all three of the declarations the row asks to drop (max-width :157, padding :159, text-align :160) are present; the recorded fix line (text-align at old :143) has only shifted to :160 because `body` above it grew a comment. The dead members are also still there: `a { font-weight: 500; color: #646cff; text-decoration: inherit }` at :113-117 and `a:hover { color: #535bf2 }` at :118-120, and the light-scheme `a:hover { color: #747bff }` at :240-242. Nothing in :113-120 or the light-scheme block has been deleted. (`h1` :147-150 and `.card` :152-154 are untouched, consistent with the row's correction that they must not be deleted unverified; the S2-C017 block at :200-206 has been replaced, not removed bare.)

frontend/src/app.css:200-206 now reads `button:focus {
 outline: none;
}
button:focus-visible {
 outline: 2px solid var(--theme-primary, #00FFFF);
 outline-offset: 2px;
}` — the block was replaced rather than recoloured, and both pseudo-classes are matched, so no button is left to the user agent's `outline-style: auto` ring on mouse focus. `grep -n outline frontend/src/app.css` shows the only other outline declarations are :231-232, a companion `.c1-collect:focus, .ro-btn:focus { outline: 2px solid var(--theme-primary, #00FFFF); outline-offset: 2px }` restoring a ring for the two programmatically focused modal buttons. Factual divergence from the row's text, recorded without judging it: the token used is `var(--theme-primary, #00FFFF)`, not the `var(--sig-cyan, #00FFFF)` the row specifies; the shape, offset and literal fallback match.
